        "id": 1000309
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-15T16:27:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Assembly code will access the memory before any Rust code runs to zero the memory. After that, any access from assembly should be via a pointer derived from the Rust reference, the same as any other variable.\n\n`static mut` would work, but I was under the impression that it was strongly discouraged in modern Rust in favour of using types with interior mutability, i.e. containing an `UnsafeCell`.",
      "parentUuid": "13001871_1868a6b7",
      "revId": "76432bc1ca82da5d305612f74a86e4140846c4f9",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
